## Why This Is Asked
New angle adds a cooldown constraint to the classic k-transaction DP, testing multi-state reasoning and recovery of the trade sequence.

## Key Concepts
- DP with cooldown using rest/hold/sold states
- Tracking transaction counts and path reconstruction
- Space optimization to O(k)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxProfitWithCooldown(prices, k) {
  const n = prices.length;
  const INF = -1e15;
  const rest = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(INF));
  const hold = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(INF));
  const sold = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(INF));
  rest[0][0] = 0;
  hold[0][0] = -prices[0];
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      rest[i][t] = Math.max(rest[i - 1][t], sold[i - 1][t]);
      hold[i][t] = Math.max(hold[i - 1][t], rest[i - 1][t] - prices[i]);
      if (t > 0) sold[i][t] = hold[i - 1][t - 1] + prices[i];
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return Math.max(...rest[n - 1]);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extract the exact trade days from the DP tables?
- How would the solution change if cooldown length varied to c days?

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces a new DP angle: exact k segments, per-segment cost, and sum-based values, requiring both interval DP and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- DP over i (prefix length) and t (blocks)
- Reconstructing endpoints from choice pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumPartition(A,k,c){
  const n=A.length;
  const P=[0];
  for(const x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const pos=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1]=(P[i]-P[0])-c, pos[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let s=t-1;s<=i-1;s++){
        const val=dp[s][t-1]+(P[i]-P[s])-c;
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; pos[i][t]=s; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let i=n, t=k;
  const blocks=[];
  while(t>0){
    const s=pos[i][t];
    blocks.push([s, i-1]);
    i=s; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {score: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model budgeted multi-interval optimization where a fixed daily cost incentivizes shorter campaigns. Requires stateful DP with reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Up to k non-overlapping subarrays
- Per-element cost transformation: B[i] = A[i] - c
- DP states: end[i][t], best[i][t]
- Recurrences: end[i][t] = max(end[i-1][t] + B[i], best[i-1][t-1] + B[i]); best[i][t] = max(best[i-1][t], end[i][t])
- Reconstruction via backpointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithCost(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const B = A.map(x => x - c);
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const best = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prevEnd = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(null));

  best[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    end[i][0] = -Infinity;
    best[i][0] = 0;
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const extend = end[i-1][t] + B[i-1];
      const startNew = best[i-1][t-1] + B[i-1];
      end[i][t] = Math.max(extend, startNew);
      if (best[i-1][t] >= end[i][t]) {
        best[i][t] = best[i-1][t];
      } else {
        best[i][t] = end[i][t];
        prevEnd[i][t] = true;
      }
    }
  }

  let bestVal = -Infinity, bestT = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
    if (best[n][t] > bestVal) { bestVal = best[n][t]; bestT = t; }
  }
  return {profit: bestVal, segments: []};
}
```

